_WIDGET ￼START_WIDGET&quot;'-ba188c9c56921a6eEND_WIDGET\" src=\"/w/images/thumb/3/3c/Ico_stats.png/25px-Ico_stats.png.webp\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"25\" height=\"25\" class=\"mw-file-element\"></picture></span><a href=\"/w/images/3/3c/Ico_stats.png\" class=\"mw-file-source\" title=\"View source image\"><!-- Image link for Crawlers --></a></span></span> <details class=\"bg3wiki-uid\">\n<summary>UID</summary>\n<code class=\"bg3wiki-uid-box\">BOOK_GLO_GeneralLoreBook_TheHalfOrcCannibalsAmongYou</code>\n</details> <span class=\"bg3wiki-uid-link\"><span class=\"mw-default-size bg3wiki-icon\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"https://bg3.norbyte.dev/search?q=name:BOOK_GLO_GeneralLoreBook_TheHalfOrcCannibalsAmongYou\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\"><img alt=\"https://bg3.norbyte.dev/search?q=name:BOOK_GLO_GeneralLoreBook_TheHalfOrcCannibalsAmongYou\" src=\"/w/images/7/70/Search_icon.svg\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"14\" height=\"14\" class=\"mw-file-element\"></a></span></span> <details class=\"bg3wiki-uid\">\n<summary>UUID</summary>\n<code class=\"bg3wiki-uid-box\">419084c9-6002-480a-a025-ae1c4580b8fe</code>\n</details> <span class=\"bg3wiki-uid-link\"><span class=\"mw-default-size bg3wiki-icon\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"https://bg3.norbyte.dev/search?q=uuid:419084c9-6002-480a-a025-ae1c4580b8fe\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\"><img alt=\"https://bg3.norbyte.dev/search?q=uuid:419084c9-6002-480a-a025-ae1c4580b8fe\" src=\"/w/images/7/70/Search_icon.svg\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"14\" height=\"14\" class=\"mw-file-element\"></a></span></span></li></ul>\n</div>   \n<div style=\"clear: both;\"></div></div>\n      <h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Text\"> Text </span></h2>\n<div class=\"bg3wiki-book-text\">\n<p>[Excerpt from Joyce Ringwarble's <i>Tusky Grins</i>\n</p><p><br>\n</p><p><br>\nWhat I don't understand is why they are not simply rounded up and sterilised. When I confront people with that idea, some nod, and smile, and make placid little comments. Some grimace or laugh and move swiftly on. Some actually recoil. And there are those who grow angry, and it is to them I relate this story:\n</p><p><br>\n</p><p><br>\nMy cousin, <span class=\"bg3wiki-icontext-icon nowrap\"><span class=\"bg3wiki-icon\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"https://forgottenrealms.fandom.com/wiki/Penelope_Ringwarble\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\"><picture><source srcset=\"/w/images/thumb/6/68/FRWiki_Icon.png/22px-FRWiki_Icon.png.webp, /w/images/thumb/6/68/FRWiki_Icon.png/33px-FRWiki_Icon.png.webp 1.5x, /w/images/thumb/6/68/FRWiki_Icon.png/44px-FRWiki_Icon.png.webp 2x\"><img alt=\"Penelope\" src=\"/w/images/thumb/6/68/FRWiki_Icon.png/22px-FRWiki_Icon.png.webp\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"22\" height=\"22\" class=\"mw-file-element\"></picture></a><a href=\"/w/images/6/68/FRWiki_Icon.png\" class=\"mw-file-source\" title=\"View source image\"><!-- Image link for Crawlers --></a></span></span> <span class=\"bg3wiki-icontext-extlink\"><a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://forgottenrealms.fandom.com/wiki/Penelope_Ringwarble\">Penelope</a></span>, spent her life championing half-orcs (and all piggy-eyed orc peoples) in her writing. She interviewed and befriended many of their kind, and one day, without warning, one of them took her daughter from her crib, and he ate her. Not gobbled up. Nothing fairytale here. He chewed the child's fingers while she screamed and waved a bloody stump.\n</p><p><br>\nAnd he smiled at my cousin.\n</p><p><br>\nThat was what drove her mad, I think. Beware, dear reader.\n</p><p><br>\n</p><p><br>\nBeware their tusky grins.\n</p>\n</div> <h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Notes\"> Notes </span></h2>\n<div class=\"bg3wiki-tooltip-box\">\n<p>See also:\n</p>\n<ul><li><span class=\"bg3wiki-icontext-block\" style=\"gap: 6px\"><span class=\"nowrap bg3wiki-icontext-icon\"><span class=\"bg3wiki-itemicon bg3wiki-itemicon-common\"><span class=\"bg3wiki-icon\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/Adopters_of_Culture\" title=\"Adopters of Culture\"><picture><source srcset=\"/w/images/thumb/f/fe/Book_Tome_X_Item_Icon.png/30px-Book_Tome_X_Item_Icon.png.webp, /w/images/thumb/f/fe/Book_Tome_X_Item_Icon.png/45px-Book_Tome_X_Item_Icon.png.webp 1.5x, /w/images/thumb/f/fe/Book_Tome_X_Item_Icon.png/60px-Book_Tome_X_Item_Icon.png.webp 2x\"><img alt=\"\" src=\"/w/images/thumb/f/fe/Book_Tome_X_Item_Icon.png/30px-Book_Tome_X_Item_Icon.png.webp\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"30\" height=\"30\" class=\"mw-file-element\"></picture></a><a href=\"/w/images/f/fe/Book_Tome_X_Item_Icon.png\" class=\"mw-file-source\" title=\"View source image\"><!-- Image link for Crawlers --></a></span></span></span><a href=\"/wiki/Adopters_of_Culture\" title=\"Adopters of Culture\">Adopters of Culture</a></span></li></ul>\n</div>   \n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20260714202325\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: [vary‐revision‐sha1, no‐toc]\nCPU time usage: 0.057 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.065 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 1905/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 34902/4194304 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 11688/4194304 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 22/200\nExpensive parser function count: 1/750\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 2/5000000 bytes\nExtLoops count: 0/1000\nLua time usage: 0.017/7.000 seconds\nLua memory usage: 977678/52428800 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%   53.411      1 Template:MiscItemPage\n100.00%   53.411      1 -total\n 40.18%   21.460      7 Template:Icon_text\n 37.12%   19.826     23 Template:Trim\n 19.84%   10.597      1 Template:Main_only\n 17.69%    9.449      2 Template:Uid\n 14.26%    7.617      1 Template:MdRarityItem\n 10.51%    5.615      1 Template:Item_icon\n 10.32%    5.513      2 Template:Template_style\n 10.22%    5.457      9 Template:Ifempty\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key bg3wiki:pc